# K03 S6 (Codex K03-CALLABLE-PATH-20261007-25, answer (c)): a path that selects a callable with a formal, written alone
# where a value is evaluated, is its application with no argument, refused as `Holder\viaPath()` is: the missing
# argument, said at the path.
Holder:
    fn: viaPath
end: Holder
fn: viaPath (int: n) int
    return: n + 1
end: viaPath
fn: run () int
    int: v Holder\viaPath
    return: v
end: run
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: run(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
